{"lines": ["A Navy warship came back from sea with claws stuck in its hull.", "The frigate USS Stein had lost its sonar, hidden in a rubber dome under the bow.", "In dry dock, the rubber was slashed. Eight percent of it, cut open.", "Inside nearly every cut, a curved hook. The kind that rings a squid's suckers.", "Except these were bigger than any squid hook ever collected.", "A petty officer named Ira Carpenter found the first one. He dug into the rubber with his knife, and it looked to him like a claw.", "He said the longest gash ran four feet.", "A Navy biologist called it a squid, but would not rule out something unknown.", "One estimate put the animal at a hundred and fifty feet. That number was never proven.", "The animal was never found. Did a giant squid leave those claws, or something nobody has named?"], "words": [["A", 0.0, 0.26], ["Navy", 0.26, 0.46], ["warship", 0.46, 1.1], ["came", 1.1, 1.3], ["back", 1.3, 1.64], ["from", 1.64, 1.88], ["sea", 1.88, 2.16], ["with", 2.16, 2.44], ["claws", 2.44, 2.78], ["stuck", 2.78, 3.26], ["in", 3.26, 3.5], ["its", 3.5, 3.62], ["hull.", 3.62, 3.84], ["The", 4.34, 4.4], ["frigate", 4.4, 4.72], ["USS", 4.72, 5.16], ["Stein", 5.16, 5.58], ["had", 5.58, 5.92], ["lost", 5.92, 6.16], ["its", 6.16, 6.38], ["sonar,", 6.38, 6.9], ["hidden", 7.26, 7.48], ["in", 7.48, 7.7], ["a", 7.7, 7.78], ["rubber", 7.78, 7.92], ["dome", 7.92, 8.28], ["under", 8.28, 8.56], ["the", 8.56, 8.72], ["bow.", 8.72, 8.92], ["In", 9.52, 9.62], ["dry", 9.62, 9.82], ["dock,", 9.82, 10.24], ["the", 10.24, 10.52], ["rubber", 10.52, 10.68], ["was", 10.68, 10.98], ["slashed.", 10.98, 11.2], ["Eight", 12.06, 12.1], ["percent", 12.1, 12.42], ["of", 12.42, 12.68], ["it,", 12.68, 12.78], ["cut", 12.78, 13.0], ["open.", 13.0, 13.34], ["Inside", 13.82, 13.9], ["nearly", 13.9, 14.4], ["every", 14.4, 14.78], ["cut,", 14.78, 15.12], ["a", 15.56, 15.66], ["curved", 15.66, 15.94], ["hook.", 15.94, 16.32], ["The", 16.8, 16.92], ["kind", 16.92, 17.16], ["that", 17.16, 17